Signal response completion before closing the daemon's socket descriptor.

Base: https://github.com/asmvik/yabai/commit/dd845723416f5fe92af49fad5ebab00369e07edd
Source: https://github.com/asmvik/yabai/blob/dd845723416f5fe92af49fad5ebab00369e07edd/src/event_loop.c#L1613

Signal subprocesses can inherit the response descriptor. Closing only the
daemon's copy leaves clients waiting for EOF until those subprocesses exit.
Shut down writes after flushing the complete response so EOF does not depend
on inherited descriptors being closed. Keep the response bytes unchanged.

--- a/src/event_loop.c
+++ b/src/event_loop.c
@@ -1633,6 +1633,7 @@
             handle_message(rsp, message);
 
             fflush(rsp);
+            shutdown(fileno(rsp), SHUT_WR);
             fclose(rsp);
 
             return;
